        "rationales": [
          {"option_id":"A","truth":"correct","derivation":"For all x>=0, y=2x+3 starts at y=3 and increases by twice the x-increase. Thus endpoint (0,3) is included, (1,5) lies on the ray and the upper-right arrow represents indefinite continuation. D_f=[0,+infinity), R_f=[3,+infinity). Both the entire candidate graph and all textual claims in A agree with f.","misconception":null},
          {"option_id":"B","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"The systematic mistake is to swap x/y in y=2x+3, derive x=2y+3 and y=(x-3)/2 correctly, but discard the inherited condition y>=0. Then allow x to be any real number. This gives precisely B's full two-arrow line through (3,0),(5,1) and points x<3, and D=R=real numbers. Its graph, formula and domains are coherent for that wrong unrestricted relation, but it is not the converse of the restricted f because g must have x>=3 and y>=0.","misconception":"Exchange the variables in the formula while dropping the source domain restriction, generating the entire supporting line and unrestricted domain/range instead of g's closed ray."},
          {"option_id":"C","truth":"correct","derivation":"Swap every pair (t,2t+3), t>=0, to (2t+3,t). In g-coordinates this is x=2y+3, y>=0, hence x>=3 and y=(x-3)/2. D_g=[3,+infinity), R_g=[0,+infinity); included endpoint (3,0) and sample (5,1) lie on the shallow ray continuing upper-right. The whole relation, its plotted ray and all displayed claims in C agree.","misconception":null},
          {"option_id":"D","truth":"incorrect","derivation":"Replace the source x>=0 by x>0 before plotting. The formula remains y=2x+3, but now the endpoint (0,3) is excluded, the plotted point is hollow, D=(0,+infinity) and R=(3,+infinity); (1,5) and the upper-right continuation remain. This operation generates the complete graph and every textual claim in D. The source includes x=0, so D is not its f.","misconception":"Read the closed lower endpoint of [0,+infinity) as an open one; carry that exclusion consistently into the graph, domain and range."}
